                "dc.subject" : [ {
                  "value" : "The Nair lab studies the neural basis of affect and emotion in the brain. The lab has uncovered neural signals in the hypothalamus that correlate with affective states of anger, sexual arousal and fear, by using new data-driven AI techniques to extract neural computations from high-dimensional neural data. These discoveries provide a first window to study how affective states are impaired in mental health disorders. \n\nThe lab also creates new AI tools to understand neural activity and behavior and is a pioneer in NeuroAI, aiming to understand how AI models may be used to understand neural computations underlying emotion.",
